---
description: AI, Agent, ASR and TTS development rules
globs:
  - "server/**/agent/**"
  - "server/**/ai/**"
  - "server/**/provider/**"
  - "contracts/schemas/**"
  - "evaluation/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

- AI providers are replaceable adapters behind project-owned interfaces.
- Prompt templates are versioned and cannot be embedded as long ad-hoc strings in business code.
- Model output must be parsed, validated against JSON Schema and then validated by business rules.
- Never use real provider calls in deterministic unit tests.
- Log provider, model, latency, token/cost metadata and validation outcome without exposing secrets.
- Retry only transient failures and invalid structured output within a bounded count.
- Provide a graceful fallback when correction, planning or evaluation generation fails.
- Learning priority and mastery transitions must not be delegated solely to an LLM.
- Any evaluation score must include confidence and explainable evidence.
